WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.562
Emperor Xuanzong heard that Li Bai was exceptionally talented, summoned him to Chang'an, and gave him a post at the Hanlin Academy. This was the most glorious period of Li Bai's life.

00:00:10.912 --> 00:00:22.691
At court, Li Bai often wrote poems for the emperor; his lines were bold and beautiful, everyone loved them, and even the emperor admired him greatly.

00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:29.870
Li Bai was free and unrestrained by nature and especially loved drinking wine; after drinking, he wrote poems faster and better.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:38.838
Legend has it that once, drunk at a banquet, he asked someone to grind ink for him and wrote beautiful lines of poetry in one breath.

00:00:39.188 --> 00:00:46.222
Witty and humorous, Li Bai left many moving stories at court, and people still tell them today.

00:00:46.572 --> 00:00:49.821
These stories made Li Bai's name ring even louder.

00:00:50.171 --> 00:00:59.608
Although Li Bai later left Chang'an, his poems have been handed down for a thousand years, and everyone remembers this 'Poet Immortal'.

